 for Celeste», «como si Charles Ives se bajara en la calle 125») y en Blue Note con Unit Structures y Conquistador! (1966). Trabaja de lavaplatos mientras gana premios; en los setenta se convierte en veterano becado y patrocinado, con conciertos de piano solo como exhibiciones atléticas, música para Baryshnikov y Alvin Ailey y la caja Berlin '88.","color":"#fb7185","family":"Free jazz y vanguardia","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/jazz/#cecil-taylor"},{"id":267285796937001,"name":"Jazz posmoderno: Murray, el World Saxophone Quartet, Zorn y Frisell","book":"Historia del jazz","author":"Ted Gioia","start":1971,"end":2010,"desc":"Eclecticismo, desconstrucción, pastiche, parodia y performance: el jazz sigue el camino de las demás artes. Carla Bley mezcla free, fusión y clásica en Escalator Over the Hill; Steve Lacy reivindica a Monk; las sesiones Wildflowers retratan el Nueva York de los lofts; Air y Henry Threadgill van de Joplin a Ayler; John Carter narra la historia afroamericana en «Roots and Folklore»; Willem Breuker evoca a Weill y Brecht. David Murray, con ciento cincuenta discos antes de los cuarenta, quiere que la música «vuelva a tener swing»; el World Saxophone Quartet (Murray, Hemphill, Lake, Bluiett) toca sin sección rítmica de Ellington al free. John Zorn, warholiano, practica el zapping sonoro: game pieces (Cobra), Morricone, Naked City. Bill Frisell pinta paisajes en pastel. Joe Lovano tiende el puente con los tradicionalistas. El compromiso político se diluye y los clubes y sellos pasan a ser galerías que deciden las modas.","color":"#94a3b8","family":"Tradicionalistas y jazz contemporáneo","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/jazz/#posmodernos"}],"book_tracks":[],"mentions":[],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"21st-Century Genre Blending","body":"Steve Lacy was cited as a contemporary artist who, in the 21st century, freely records in \"whatever idiom they like,\" reflecting a shift where genre mixing is no longer revolutionary but expected. \"artists record in whatever idiom they like, from Lil Nas X to Steve Lacey.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"What’s 1984 Got to Do with It Edition Part 1","url":null}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":202304019687684,"type":"album","name":"Reflections: Steve Lacy Plays Thelonious Monk","list_id":56169400631168,"list":"RYM Top — Jazz — Post-Bop","src":"musthear","rank":198,"year":1959,"note":null,"yt":"po0J3j5eN2M","scaruffi":null},{"id":117823768372139,"type":"album","name":"The Straight Horn of Steve Lacy","list_id":56169400631168,"list":"RYM Top — Jazz — Post-Bop","src":"musthear","rank":175,"year":1962,"note":null,"yt":"6NX02DEAZws","scaruffi":null},{"id":61130644077518,"type":"album","name":"Moon","list_id":63979376183344,"list":"RYM Top — Experimental — Free Improvisation","src":"musthear","rank":111,"year":1971,"note":null,"yt":"sj8uZqVtDbE","scaruffi":null},{"id":61130644077518,"type":"album","name":"Moon","list_id":8160780515432,"list":"RYM Top — Jazz — Free Jazz","src":"musthear","rank":191,"year":1971,"note":null,"yt":"sj8uZqVtDbE","scaruffi":null},{"id":239077332713571,"type":"album","name":"Lumps","list_id":230989056896710,"list":"RYM Top — Jazz — European Free Jazz","src":"musthear","rank":64,"year":1978,"note":null,"yt":"iFFZseKRNts","scaruffi":null},{"id":130856025993295,"type":"album","name":"Apollo XXI","list_id":147465301620623,"list":"RYM Top — Psychedelia — Psychedelic Soul","src":"musthear","rank":177,"year":2019,"note":null,"yt":"LW2CqGGUJh4","scaruffi":null},{"id":226870166843362,"type":"song","name":"Bad Habit","work_year":2022,"list_id":184225487175112,"list":"Billboard Hot 100 nº1 · 2020s","src":"singles","rank":1142,"year":2022,"note":"3 semanas","yt":"VF-FGf_ZZiI","scaruffi":null},{"id":226870166843362,"type":"song","name":"Bad Habit","work_year":2022,"list_id":260042115848106,"list":"Billboard Year-End 2022","src":"singles","rank":28,"year":2022,"note":